<div class="wrap two"><article class="prose">
<h2>Why a timeline matters</h2>
<p>Property claims carry several clocks at once. Some come from the policy, such as proof of loss, the window to name an appraiser and the replacement-cost recovery period. Others, like the suit-limitation period, can end your options if they pass unnoticed.</p>
<h2>Setting the windows</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Proof of loss:</strong> if the carrier requested one, enter the request date. The deadline is counted from that date.</li>
<li><strong>Appraiser naming:</strong> counted here from the date of loss as a planning placeholder. Once a demand is sent, count from the demand date.</li>
<li><strong>Suit limitation:</strong> read your policy’s “Suit Against Us” condition and ask an Arkansas attorney how it applies.</li></ul>
<p>The .ics file works with Google Calendar, Apple Calendar and Outlook. It’s generated in your browser; nothing is uploaded.</p>
<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Are the default numbers Arkansas law?<svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. They are placeholders. Your policy and Arkansas law control, and an attorney can confirm deadlines.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does invoking appraisal stop the suit clock?<svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Don’t assume so. Ask an attorney about your specific situation if a deadline is approaching.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is my date stored anywhere?<svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. Everything runs in your browser and disappears when you close the page.</p></div></details></div>
